# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ai-bunker — .gitignore
#
# Two rules decide what lives here:
#   1. Anything that names a machine, a secret, or a model choice is generated,
#      never committed. The *brief* is committed; the *engine* is not.
#   2. Anything measured (token counts, benchmarks, logs) is a run artifact.
#      The script that measures is committed; its output is not.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Personal scratch notes, working thread, assessments (do not commit)
.private/

# --- Sovereignty: secrets and machine-specific resolutions -----------------
# The committed brief says what the workload NEEDS (llm.brief.yaml).
# The engine file says what THIS machine resolved it to — machine-specific.
llm.engine*.yaml
*.engine.yaml
env.sh
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
config/config.yaml
config/gateway.yaml
config/*.local.yaml
!config/*.example.yaml
secrets/
*.pem
*.key
!**/public*.key
.netrc

# --- Measurement artifacts -------------------------------------------------
logs/
reports/
bench/results/
*.report.md
*.report.json
context_cost*.json
cout_reel*.json

# --- Python ----------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.Python
build/
develop-eggs/
dist/
downloads/
eggs/
.eggs/
lib64/
parts/
sdist/
var/
wheels/
share/python-wheels/
*.egg-info/
.installed.cfg
*.egg
MANIFEST
pip-log.txt
pip-delete-this-directory.txt

# Virtual environments
.venv/
venv/
ENV/
env/
.conda/

# Test / coverage / type / lint caches
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.dmypy.json
dmypy.json
.pyre/
.pytype/
.hypothesis/
.tox/
.nox/
htmlcov/
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml
*.cover
nosetests.xml
.deepeval/

# Notebooks
.ipynb_checkpoints/
profile_default/
ipython_config.py

# The site's built stylesheet is committed on purpose: deployment is a file
# upload, and requiring Node on the far end to regenerate it would make the
# site undeployable by the person who owns it.
!web/css/app.css

# --- Node (OpenCode / Claude Code client plugins) --------------------------
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*
.npm/

# --- Models and weights ----------------------------------------------------
# Never in git. They come from the registry at serve time.
*.gguf
*.safetensors
*.bin
!**/tiny*.bin
models/weights/
.ollama/
.cache/huggingface/

# --- Editors and OS --------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
ehthumbs.db
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
!.vscode/settings.shared.json

# --- Agent harness local state ---------------------------------------------
.opencode/node_modules/
.opencode/bun.lock*
opencode.db
.claude/settings.local.json
.agents/

# The film: source is tracked, output is not.
# `video/film/index.html` plus `video/film/narration/` rebuild the MP4 exactly
# (`npx hyperframes render`), and `video/film.yaml` is what keeps the numbers
# in it true. The render itself is tens of megabytes of derived bytes and has
# no business in a repository that has to stay cloneable.
video/film/out/
video/film/renders/
video/film/.hyperframes/
video/film/node_modules/
*.mp4
